I think it should work like this.  The henchman goes off wandering.  During
this time, he is mapping the dungeon, but you don't get to see it.  When
you meet him again, #chatting him causes the newly explored regions to be
revealed.

Or maybe instead of chatting, he will hand you a scroll, or else he could
just yell at you from remote locations, so you would in fact see it being
mapped out as he explores.

That introduces some new dangers -- perhaps you could be deafened by
loud noises.  If you and your henchman communicate via speech, you'd lose
that, temporarily or whatever.  There could be certain kinds of monsters
the henchman will always attack, and some that he won't.  You should
definitely be able to swap spaces with him.

Hmmm.  perhaps there could be female hench-persons?

